{"skill":{"slug":"gh-issues","displayName":"gh-issues"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1774453481689,"changelog":"Initial registration","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":34564,"sha256":"6b18eeeba4294505a986bed7a51b2f74766465c4b78fa094e02654e5bb96e90e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2344,"sha256":"e7069993aef2b53b3750a2a75ea35d6086e80040e2c3cf538eabef5b278daf9a","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789436067817,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2fc2d497f2f4fd6065e4b6e95081d2e669a457b7d51020ada877c68e497f8fd6","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2fc2d497f2f4fd6065e4b6e95081d2e669a457b7d51020ada877c68e497f8fd6","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090105481},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":29,"checkedAt":1789436067817},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill automates GitHub fixes and PRs, but it exposes GitHub tokens and can make unattended repository and global Git changes.","dimensions":[{"detail":"GitHub API access is expected, but the instructions read GH_TOKEN from local config files, print the full token or token prefix, use raw shell templates with unescaped values, and optionally send PR summaries to Telegram.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact metadata requires and offers to install gh, while the runtime instructions repeatedly say gh is not used and curl is used instead. This is inconsistent but not the main security concern.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Issue bodies, titles, PR bodies, and review comments are injected into privileged sub-agent prompts without clear untrusted-data boundaries. The --yes, --watch, and --cron paths can reduce or remove interactive approval before code changes are pushed.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill writes claim and cursor state under /data/.clawdbot for automation, keeps sub-agent transcripts, persists tokens in Git remote URLs, and modifies global Git credential helper configuration without restoration.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core purpose is coherent with the description: fetch issues, spawn agents, push branches, open PRs, and address reviews. The concern is the breadth of write authority over repositories and public PR/comment actions, especially when driven by remote issue and review content.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use only with a narrowly scoped GitHub token and a repository you are comfortable letting an agent modify. Avoid --yes, --cron, and --notify-channel unless you have an external approval process. If this has already been run, check .git/config and global Git credential settings for token-bearing remotes or changed helpers, and rotate the token if it may have appeared in logs or transcripts.","findings":"[SSD-3] unexpected: Confirmed. SKILL.md instructs token echoing and token-prefix verification while sub-agent cleanup is set to keep transcripts; disclosing any part of GH_TOKEN is not needed for issue automation.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Partially confirmed. PR creation is described, but local credential-file access, third-party Telegram notification, and the practical scope of write actions are not prominently disclosed enough for the authority requested.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Confirmed. The manifest requires and installs gh, while the runtime instructions say there is no gh CLI dependency; this is an operational inconsistency rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[EA2] expected: Automation and sub-agent spawning fit the purpose, but --yes and --cron allow unattended commit, push, PR, and comment actions based on external GitHub content, so the control model is weak.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Confirmed. The skill reads GH_TOKEN from ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json and /data/.clawdbot/openclaw.json rather than relying only on injected environment state, expanding credential exposure.\n[E1] expected: GitHub API traffic is expected for this skill. Optional Telegram notification is disclosed by flag, but users should understand it sends repository and PR summary data to an external channel.\n[RA2] expected: The reported persistence is mostly disclosed claim/cursor tracking and watch-mode state, not a hidden backdoor. Cron fire-and-forget operation still increases unattended automation risk.\n[T01] unexpected: Confirmed. Remote GitHub issue and review text is passed into agents that have shell, repository write, GH_TOKEN, push, PR, and comment capabilities, with no explicit instruction to treat that text as untrusted.\n[T09] unexpected: Confirmed. The artifact contains token printing, token-bearing Git remote URLs, and unvalidated interpolation into shell commands and JSON payloads.\n[T05] unexpected: Confirmed. The push workflow runs git config --global credential.helper \"\" and does not preserve or restore the prior global Git setting.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789436067817}}}}}